    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That Pitx1 was sequenced from these Miocene fish.",
        "does_not_claim: That the centimetre-scale fossil photograph is a 42 µm histological section.",
        "does_not_claim: That the unguided stripe field reproduces the skeleton. Its CV is 58.1; the 92.3 score is the registered render.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Chronoseries (Dv/Du, γ) = (14.2, 1.55), (18, 1), (24.8, 0.62) giving 32.14, 41.94, 56.90 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Du ±10% band 39.80 / 41.94 / 44.02 µm, pure-field CV 58.1 beside registered CV 92.3, bone-mask KS.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian at (a, b) = (0.062, 1.18), σ(k), and Du bisection onto 41.94 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: Bell & Haglund 1982 and Hunt, Bell & Travis 2008: directional pelvic reduction in Truckee Fm G. doryssus.",
        "reported_in_source: Kondo & Asai 1995: reaction-diffusion waves set pigment spacing on fish skin.",
        "reported_in_source: Shapiro et al. 2004 and Chan et al. 2010: extant pelvic reduction maps to a Pitx1 enhancer deletion.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion: a critical wavenumber selected by diffusion and reaction rates.",
        "reported_in_source: Voje, Bell & Stuart 2022: CC BY 4.0 plate of weakly and strongly armored G. doryssus morphs.",
        "transfer_boundary: 42 µm melanophore spacing is transferred from extant pigment-pattern RD onto a fossil that preserves bone, not chromatophores." ;
